## 6. g25-fu-x: what the protocol and the other crates need from this task
## - mixdog-app-protocol (rows/pending-rows/g25-fu-x.rows): PcAccessReadiness.needsEnroll (the Rust type is edited; regenerate schema/client_methods.json and packages/protocol/src/index.ts).
## - The phone's screen control (s3-screen-source, G7) consumes PcAccessService::approve_with_credential(CredentialRequest{client_id, public_key, credential, cancelled}) -> CredentialAnswer{outcome: Busy | Ran(KeyOutcome), state, detail}
##   through its ScreenPcAccess port (mixdog-tools computer_screen/session.rs): `cancelled` is the session's AbortSignal::aborted, `outcome` maps by KeyOutcome::name() (the port's CredentialResult.outcome is the kebab name, `busy` for Busy),
##   and `state` is HelperState (the port's InstallState). The same PcAccessInstaller instance (production_installer) is the one the lease's InstallPort must use, so the one in-flight latch covers both.
